Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||02-21-2000||01:12 AM||||To: Mshill and 1fst2m6.<P>How do you like your Eibachs?<BR>Any problems?<BR>Any props?||||reg||10
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-21-2000||08:43 AM||||LOVE every minute of them... they can be BEAT TO HELL and still perform superbly! (at the strip running mid 13s or pulling over 1 full G on a skid pad) I also have them on a set of Koni shocks/struts. I'd like for it to be lower and a bit more stiff. but i drive her REALLY hard... got all my suspension stuff from <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  ordered them on monday had them thursday! You might also want to try <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  , <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  , or <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cyberauto.com</A>   their great for daily driver/weekend warrior! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||02-21-2000||06:05 PM||||Mine are on my 86GT which is not in use at this time.  I only know that the guy I bought it from put Eibachs and 60 series tires on 15 inch rims and the car is really low to the ground.  I am not driving it because it isn't registered or smogged and I am int he middle of rebuilding my 86SE.  When I get the SE out of the garage and on the road the GT goes into the garage for some work and then I will get it smogged and registered.<P>I decided against the Eibachs on the SE because it will be a daily driver and I don't want to have the nose or underside messed up on a speed bump or a high curb in a parking lot.  I am still looking for a 1 inch drop for it though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||02-21-2000||07:02 PM||||Thanks for your replys!<P>1fst2m6: You think they need to be stiffer?<BR>I think they are plenty stiff! In mine if you take a hard turn and it has some rutts it skips a bit. I think they are a titch bit hard but I like them very much!<P>mshill: I've had my Eibachs for about two months and Ive looked for stuff to get into trouble but I've never scraped or bottomed out, in this respect the Eibachs are great!<P>Are your springs on the rear loose when you jack it up? On mine when you jack up the rear you can move the sring out of the perch.<BR>I installed them myself and am wondering if I missed something. I have Eibach springs and KYB shocks! Also a rear Addco sway bar.<p>[This message has been edited by FIEROCIOUS (edited 02-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||02-21-2000||08:50 PM||||I haven't had my GT up on jacks yet.  I also have the Eibachs with KYB shocks and struts.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-22-2000||08:20 AM||||I wish the rear springs were stiffer... just cause of the setup i'm running. With the nitrous on the rear suspension will bottom out... but thats not really the springs fault.. even with the Koni full tight they still collapse. but for normal driving.. Love them! ||||reg||1
